      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database connection is persistently failing with an authentication error (`Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`), so I cannot execute verification queries. I have retried multiple times across different tables. I will therefore finalize the SQL based entirely on the semantic-network evidence, which is strong and unambiguous for this task.\n\n---\n\n## Report\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (gold, per hints and confirmed via semantic_get):**\n- **LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — one row per subject per term within library reserve scope. Key columns: `SUBJECT_ID` (\"joins to TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\"), `OFFER_DEPT_NAME` (\"Offering department name, e.g. 'Mathematics'\"), `TERM_CODE`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`. The hint maps \"department\" → `OFFER_DEPT_NAME` here.\n- **TIP_DETAIL** — one row per subject-material-status combination per term. Key columns: `SUBJECT_ID` (\"joins to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID, SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\"), `RECORD_COUNT` (\"Number of material records for this subject/material combination; used in material-count statistics\"), `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY`, `TERM_CODE`. The hint maps \"TIP material\" → `SUBJECT_ID`, `RECORD_COUNT` here.\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — one row per subject per term (rollup of sections). Key columns: `SUBJECT_ID` (\"joins to TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID and LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\"), `TERM_CODE`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (\"Number of students enrolled in the subject\"), `TOTAL_UNITS` (\"Total credit units of the subject\"), `OFFER_DEPT_NAME`. The hint maps \"average enrollment\" → `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, \"terms\" → `TERM_CODE`, \"total units\" → `TOTAL_UNITS` here.\n\n**Related tables investigated (not needed for final SQL):** TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (TIP program subject scope; parent of TIP_DETAIL — not in gold list), SUBJECT_SUMMARY (registrar final enrollment; hint doesn't map any field to it), SUBJECT_OFFERED (section grain; would need aggregation), TIP_MATERIAL / TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS (material bibliographics/status decoding — question doesn't ask for status filtering), LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL (library reserve items — question asks about TIP materials, not library reserves).\n\n**Metrics:**\n- **dw_1766** — exact same task shape: \"the highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department\". Its gold SQL uses a two-level aggregation: inner CTE `GROUP BY DEPARTMENT_NAME, TERM_CODE` computing `AVG(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)`, outer `MAX(avg_enrollment_per_term)` per department. It also joins through LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\n- **dw_1973** — precedent for \"at least one associated TIP material\": implemented as an `INNER JOIN TIP_DETAIL` on SUBJECT_ID (existence semantics).\n\n**Concepts / Column concepts:**\n- **concept_course_material_programs** — TIP and library reserve programs \"linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE\"; decision guide: textbook-material questions → TIP tables; library-scope enrollment → LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\n- **concept_subject_offering_facts** — decision guide: \"Questions about subject-level units with offering department/school … Use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, which carries both TOTAL_UNITS and OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME\" — confirms SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY as the right source for TOTAL_UNITS + enrollment at subject/term grain.\n- **column_concept_enrollment_measures** — decision guide: \"Questions about number of enrolled students per subject offering or per department totals: Use NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS from SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject grain)\". Matches the hint mapping exactly.\n- **column_concept_total_units** — decision guide: \"Unit statistics at subject-offering rollup level with offering department/school: Use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS.\"\n- **column_concept_subject_id** — SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format; decision guide: \"Joining textbook materials or library reserves to catalog/summary subject attributes: Match on SUBJECT_ID\".\n- **column_concept_department_name** — \"Filtering by department in section-level, textbook-program, or library analysis: Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of … LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\"\n- **column_concept_term_code**, **column_concept_material_status_key** — term join key semantics; TIP status domain (no status filter required by this question).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\nFrom `semantic_graph` on TIP_DETAIL: outgoing joins to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_MATERIAL, TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS, ACADEMIC_TERMS(_ALL), COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY; incoming joins from LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL, SUBJECT_OFFERED, IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL. Concept membership: concept_course_material_programs. Column concepts: term_code, subject_id, material_status_key. This confirms the documented join edges `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID ↔ TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID` and `SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID ↔ TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID` given in the hints (also stated verbatim in the column definitions retrieved via semantic_get).\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Enrollment measure candidates** (evidence: column_concept_enrollment_measures comparisons):\n| Dimension | SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS | SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Grain | per subject per term | per subject per term (library scope) | per subject/cluster per term |\n| Meaning | headcount at subject grain | library-program snapshot | official registrar enrollment |\n| Coverage | all offered subjects | only library-reserve-scope subjects | all subjects |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping:**\nAtomic requirements: (R1) department per offering course → LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME (hint-mapped; SUPPORTED); (R2) average enrollment measure → SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (hint-mapped; SUPPORTED — decision guide endorses it for \"number of enrolled students per subject offering\"); (R3) per-term grouping → SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE (SUPPORTED); (R4) \"at least one associated TIP material\" → INNER JOIN TIP_DETAIL on SUBJECT_ID + RECORD_COUNT >= 1 (SUPPORTED per dw_1973 precedent and TIP_DETAIL.RECORD_COUNT definition); (R5) TOTAL_UNITS > 0 → SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS (SUPPORTED; LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED and TIP_DETAIL have NO units columns — NOT-SUPPORTED there per retrieved column lists); (R6) two-level max-of-per-term-average → dw_1766 precedent shape (SUPPORTED).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"department offering a course\" → `OFFER_DEPT_NAME` (column_concept_department_name decision guide names LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME for library analysis; hint confirms). \"at least one associated TIP material\" → existence of TIP_DETAIL rows with `RECORD_COUNT >= 1` (hint maps \"TIP material\" to TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID + RECORD_COUNT). \"average enrollment among all terms\" → AVG of SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS per TERM_CODE, then MAX across terms (dw_1766 anchors this exact phrase \"highest average number of enrolled students in any term\" to the two-level pattern). \"total units … greater than 0\" → SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS > 0 (only gold table with a units column).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** max-of-per-term-average-enrollment precedents: 1 — dw_1766 (two-level AVG per dept+term then MAX, joined through LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED). \"at least one TIP material\" precedents: dw_1973 (INNER JOIN TIP_DETAIL on SUBJECT_ID).\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED: consumed by dw_1766 (department-level enrollment averages), dw_3911, dw_3248, dw_1288; serves library-scope subject/department questions; parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.\n- TIP_DETAIL: consumed by dw_1973, dw_3973, dw_2895, dw_3612, dw_4558; serves \"does subject have textbook material / how many material records\" questions via RECORD_COUNT and TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY.\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY: consumed by dw_3632, dw_4184, dw_4305 and unit-statistics metrics (dw_3901, dw_3644); serves subject-per-term enrollment and unit questions with offering department attribution.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓, semantic_graph (via TIP_DETAIL neighbors) ✓, mysql_query ✗ (DB access denied)\n- TIP_DETAIL — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓, semantic_graph query_neighbors ✓, mysql_query ✗\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓, graph ✓, mysql_query ✗\n- dw_1766, dw_1973 — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get (full SQL) ✓\n- concept_course_material_programs, concept_subject_offering_facts — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓\n- column_concept_enrollment_measures, column_concept_total_units, column_concept_subject_id, column_concept_department_name, column_concept_term_code, column_concept_material_status_key — semantic_search ✓, semantic_get ✓ (term_code/material_status_key via search desc + graph edges)\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_MATERIAL, TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS, LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL — semantic_search ✓, desc-level review ✓; excluded (not in gold list, no hint mapping, question doesn't require their fields)\n\n**Note:** `mysql_query` failed on every attempt with `Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost' (using password: YES)` — an infrastructure/credential error, not a SQL error. Execution verification was therefore impossible; the query is validated against retrieved column definitions and gold-SQL precedents instead.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:** LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME (department, per hint + department_name decision guide); TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID/RECORD_COUNT (TIP-material existence filter, per hint + dw_1973 precedent); SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID/TERM_CODE/NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS/TOTAL_UNITS (course-term grain measure and units filter, per hint + enrollment/total_units decision guides).\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** Two-level aggregation exactly per dw_1766: inner query joins the three tables on SUBJECT_ID (the two hint-documented join edges), filters `t.RECORD_COUNT >= 1` and `s.TOTAL_UNITS > 0`, groups by department + TERM_CODE computing `AVG(s.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)`; outer query takes `MAX()` of that per-term average per department. No ROUND (question forbids rounded answers). Caveat: joining TIP_DETAIL directly can fan out rows per subject (multiple material rows), which weights the AVG — this matches the gold join structure given in the hints and the dw_1766 precedent style, so it is retained deliberately.\n\n**6c. Three-perspective reasons:**\n- **Data perspective:** SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY is one row per subject per term (retrieved granularity), so AVG per TERM_CODE is well-defined; LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED and TIP_DETAIL lack any units column (retrieved column lists), so TOTAL_UNITS > 0 can only be applied on SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY; SUBJECT_ID is the documented cross-table join key in all three tables' column descriptions.\n- **Semantic-network perspective:** graph edges confirm LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED → TIP_DETAIL and SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY → TIP_DETAIL joins on SUBJECT_ID; column_concept decision guides explicitly route \"enrolled students per subject offering\" to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS and subject-level unit statistics to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS; concept_course_material_programs routes material-existence questions to TIP_DETAIL.\n- **Business perspective:** dw_1766 is a same-shape gold precedent (\"highest average number of enrolled students in any term\") using the identical two-level AVG-then-MAX pattern through LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED; dw_1973 establishes \"at least one associated TIP material\" as an inner join to TIP_DETAIL.\n\n**6d. Alternatives:** Using LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS instead would follow dw_1766's measure source, but the hint explicitly maps \"average enrollment\" to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS and \"terms\" to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE — the hint mapping is the tie-breaker.\n\n**Final SQL:**\n\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS (\n    SELECT l.OFFER_DEPT_NAME,\n           s.TERM_CODE,\n           AVG(s.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS avg_enrollment_per_term\n    FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED l\n    INNER JOIN TIP_DETAIL t ON l.SUBJECT_ID = t.SUBJECT_ID\n    INNER JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY s ON s.SUBJECT_ID = t.SUBJECT_ID\n    WHERE t.RECORD_COUNT >= 1\n      AND s.TOTAL_UNITS > 0\n    GROUP BY l.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, s.TERM_CODE\n)\nSELECT OFFER_DEPT_NAME,\n       MAX(avg_enrollment_per_term) AS max_avg_enrollment\nFROM inner_cte\nGROUP BY OFFER_DEPT_NAME;\n```\n\nSELECT list check: the question asks for (1) the department and (2) the maximum average enrollment — exactly 2 columns, in that order. ✓\n\n",
